# Audit scripts are downloaded straight from the site and executed. Line-ending
# normalisation breaks them, so pin the endings each interpreter requires.
#
#   PowerShell tolerates LF, but a CRLF file opened in Notepad on the candidate's
#   machine must not collapse into one line.
#   bash/zsh refuse a script whose shebang line ends in CR ("bad interpreter: ^M").
*.ps1 text eol=crlf
*.sh  text eol=lf
